  "body": "Chrome ignores registerProtocolHandler requests if they are not issued by user gestures. In chrome, this is evaluated based on the frame's [UserActivation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#tracking-user-activation) state. \r\n\r\nI believe that Firefox has the same requirement.\r\n\r\nI couldn't find in the [custom handlers spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#custom-handlers) any reference to this requirement. \r\n\r\nShouldn't we add it explicitly ? It seems there are good reasons (eg confusing user experience; see bugs [119438](https://crbug.com/119438),  [62799](https://crbug.com/62799) and [724919](https://crbug.com/724919) for details)",
